<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <Flow> breaks `sf`
        deploy at source conversion with the misleading error "unable to find matching parent
        xml file". Precedent: flows/Counter_Offer_Notify.

        =====================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-14 (Phase 3, observation 7). THIS FILE WAS NOT IN THE SPEC, NOT IN
        THE REQUIREMENTS DOC AND NOT IN THE BUILD BRIEF. IT WAS FOUND BY SWEEPING flows/ FOR
        Negotiation_Status__c, AND LEFT ALONE IT WOULD HAVE FAILED SILENTLY AND PERMANENTLY.
        =====================================================================

        WHAT IT DOES. After-save on Contract_Review__c: notifies the Acquisitions_Team group that
        a PSA is ready for signature. doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria = true, so it fires
        on the TRANSITION INTO the value, not on every subsequent save.

        THE DEFECT. Its only entry criterion was Negotiation_Status__c = 'Ready for Execution',
        with NO record-type criterion, so it has always served BOTH PSA record types. Phase 3
        gives Acquisition_PSA its own sequence - Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed -> Executed - and
        removes 'Ready for Execution' from that record type. Every acquisition PSA would then
        pass from Negotiation straight to Signed to Executed WITHOUT EVER MATCHING THIS FLOW, so
        the "PSA ready for execution" notification would stop reaching the Acquisitions team for
        every acquisition deal, for ever, with nothing erroring and no test failing. A
        notification that stops arriving is indistinguishable from a quiet week.

        THE FIX AND WHY IT IS AN OR RATHER THAN A SWAP. 'Signed' is the acquisition analogue of
        'Ready for Execution' - the document is final and signatures are being collected, the
        step immediately before 'Executed' in both sequences. But Disposition_PSA STILL RUNS ON
        'Ready for Execution' and is untouched by Phase 3 (decision O3), so swapping the literal
        would simply move the outage onto the sell-side path. filterLogic is therefore 'or' over
        both values. This is additive and correct on BOTH sides of the Phase 3 row migration, so
        it ships at P3-D1 rather than in the migration window.

        ⚠ THE TWO VALUES ARE MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE IN PRACTICE - no record type exposes both - so
        the OR cannot double-notify. Disposition_PSA's behaviour is byte-for-byte unchanged: it
        can never reach 'Signed'.
        🔴 BOTH SENTENCES IN THIS PARAGRAPH ARE RETRACTED 2026-08-21 - see the dated block below.
        They were true from 2026-08-14 until a live Setup edit on 2026-08-21 changed the premise.

        ⚠ THE NOTIFICATION TITLE IS DELIBERATELY NOT REWORDED. "PSA ready for execution" reads
        correctly for 'Signed' as well as for 'Ready for Execution', and it is shared by both
        record types; rewording it to name one sequence's vocabulary would make it wrong for the
        other. Same reasoning as the Stage__c labels (PSA Drafting / Review / Contract Execution)
        being left buy-side-shaped in Disposition_PSA's own header.
        ⚠ AMENDED 2026-08-21: "shared by both record types" is no longer true in practice - see
        below - but the title itself is UNCHANGED and this reasoning still explains why it was
        never record-type-flavoured wording to begin with.

        ⚠ 'Executed' IS DELIBERATELY NOT ADDED HERE. It is the handoff, owned by
        ContractExecutionService, and it already has its own downstream notifications.

        =====================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-21. THE USER CHANGED Disposition_PSA.Negotiation_Status__c DIRECTLY IN
        SETUP THE SAME DAY (see the record type file's own header for the full measurement). THE
        PREMISE THIS FLOW'S SHARED-'Signed'-VALUE DESIGN RESTED ON IS GONE, AND THE USER HAS
        EXPLICITLY DECLINED A SELL-SIDE REPLACEMENT NOTIFICATION FOR NOW.
        =====================================================================

        RETRACTED, verbatim, from the paragraph above: "Disposition_PSA STILL RUNS ON 'Ready for
        Execution'" and "Disposition_PSA's behaviour is byte-for-byte unchanged: it can never
        reach 'Signed'." Disposition_PSA now runs Initial Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed. It no
        longer reaches 'Ready for Execution' at all, and 'Signed' is now its TERMINAL, shared with
        Acquisition_PSA's pre-terminal 'Signed'. Left alone, every disposition PSA reaching
        'Signed' would trigger this exact notification - "PSA ready for execution", to
        Acquisitions_Team - which is wrong on both counts for a sell-side deal: the recipient
        group is the buy-side team, and "ready for execution" describes a step that no longer
        exists on this record type (the deal moves straight to Closing from Signed).

        THE FIX, RESTORING RATHER THAN CHANGING ACQUISITION BEHAVIOUR. Before 2026-08-21 a
        disposition PSA could never reach 'Signed', so in PRACTICE this flow only ever fired for
        acquisition rows despite having no explicit scope. A third filter was added -
        Opportunity__c IS NOT NULL - AND'd with the existing OR, making that practice explicit
        rather than accidental: `(1 OR 2) AND 3`. The Acquisitions Team's observable behaviour is
        UNCHANGED - it still receives exactly the notifications it received before this edit,
        because every row that previously matched (1 OR 2) already had Opportunity__c populated
        (OpportunityReviewService is the only creator of acquisition Contract Reviews and always
        stamps it; Disposition_PSA rows never carry it - Disposition_PSA's own record type header
        states "Opportunity__c stays blank, and that blank is load-bearing"). No sell-side
        notification was added, per explicit user decision.

        🔴 THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE LOOKUP, NOT RecordType.DeveloperName, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE,
        NOT THE DEFAULT. Two considerations, weighed on the merits for this file specifically:
        (a) precedent - Contract_Review__c.Disposition__c's own field header already states the
        house rule for this exact object family: "THE LOOKUP, NOT THE RECORD TYPE, IS THE
        DISCRIMINATOR anything outside the record page should test" - flows/Counter_Offer_Notify
        and flows/PSA_Version_Notify both already key on the lookup for the same reason, on child
        objects of this one; (b) the field IS a zero-hop, direct field on the SAME object this
        flow triggers on (Contract_Review__c itself carries Opportunity__c), so - unlike those two
        precedents, which were forced into <filterFormula> by a two-hop limitation - the plain
        <filters>/<filterLogic> builder syntax already used by this file could express it directly
        with no new element type. Kept the existing shape rather than switching to
        <filterFormula>, which is the more conservative edit of the two. RecordType.DeveloperName
        was considered and rejected: it has zero precedent anywhere in flows/ (even as a filter
        field on the triggering object itself, not just via a relationship hop) and would exclude
        Master-type Contract Reviews, which decision O3 deliberately keeps eligible for
        'Ready for Execution' - see the next paragraph.

        ⚠ THE 'Ready for Execution' FILTER BRANCH IS KEPT, NOT REMOVED, AND THIS WAS A CLOSE CALL.
        Live-checked via the UI API before this edit: neither Acquisition_PSA
        (Draft, Negotiation, Signed, Executed) nor Disposition_PSA (Initial Draft, Negotiation,
        Signed) exposes 'Ready for Execution' any more, so in the CURRENT org this branch is dead
        for both record types. It is NOT removed because the value stays ACTIVE on the field
        permanently under decision O3 (Disposition_PSA's record type header, unchanged by this
        pass), and a MASTER-type Contract Review - the shape TestDataFactory produces when a
        record type is absent or unavailable, e.g. in a fresh scratch org - is not constrained by
        either record type's allow-list and can still legitimately be written with
        'Ready for Execution' today. Removing the branch would silently stop notifying on that one
        remaining population for zero benefit; keeping it costs nothing, since it can never
        double-fire with 'Signed' (still mutually exclusive against any row this flow's Opportunity
        gate now admits). Revisit if decision O3 is ever revisited.
    -->
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Notify_Ready</name>
        <label>Notify Ready</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <actionName>GroupNotifier</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>recipientGroup</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Acquisitions_Team</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>title</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>PSA ready for execution</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>body</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Name</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>targetRecordId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>GroupNotifier</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>PSA Ready Notify {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>PSA Ready Notify</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Notify_Ready</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>(1 OR 2) AND 3</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Negotiation_Status__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Ready for Execution</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Negotiation_Status__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Signed</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Opportunity__c</field>
            <operator>IsNull</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Contract_Review__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
